-- Phase-D note on rule form: the structural rules below state their
-- premises with `>` (hypothesis binders), not `->` inside the formula.
-- MM0's logic has no internal modus ponens — a `->`-inside-formula axiom
-- only proves that an *implication term* is derivable, and can never be
